  {
   "id": "E03",
   "question": "When do I create an installment plan?",
   "type": "answerable",
   "expected_status": "answered",
   "expected_card": "M2C-24",
   "evidence_expected": "You create an installment plan when both of the following apply",
   "http_status": 200,
   "status": "answered",
   "selected_card": "M2C-24",
   "public_card_id": "M2C-24",
   "card_title": "Creating Installment Plans",
   "pipeline_status": "answered",
   "reason_code": null,
   "page": [
    "9442486404b54071b4ebeab6a16628e7/790dc5536a51204be10000000a174cb4"
   ],
   "answer": "You create an installment plan when both of the following apply: [S1]\n- There are one or more open items on the contract account of a business partner. [S1]\nRegardless of whether you have the system create an installment plan proposal by entering the installment amount or by entering the rounding amount and number of installments, there may be a remaining amount when the individual installments are calculated. [S3]\n- Create or delete an installment plan surcharge and/or an inflation surcharge The prerequisite in this case is that you activated the enhancement in Customizing under Business Transactions > Deferral and Installment Plans > Activate Installment Plan Enhancement for Charges/Interest . [S4]",
